WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:10.818
Hi! What is one third plus one sixth? The denominators are different, so we can't add them straight away. Let's learn how.

2
00:00:10.968 --> 00:00:13.794
First, let's draw one third.

3
00:00:13.944 --> 00:00:23.826
One third is the same as two sixths. Since 6 is a multiple of 3, we change one third into two sixths by multiplying the top and bottom by 2.

4
00:00:23.976 --> 00:00:33.090
Now the denominators match: two sixths plus one sixth is three sixths. Keep the denominator, and add only the numerators.

5
00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:38.802
Finally, simplify: three sixths is one half.

6
00:00:38.952 --> 00:00:48.306
Three quarters minus three eighths: change three quarters into six eighths, then subtract three eighths. The answer is three eighths.

7
00:00:48.456 --> 00:00:55.458
We can subtract from 1 as well: 1 is twelve twelfths, minus five twelfths gives seven twelfths.

8
00:00:55.608 --> 00:01:05.370
If the answer is more than 1, write it as a mixed number: five sixths plus two thirds is nine sixths, which is 1 and a half.

9
00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:10.530
Watch out! One third plus one sixth is not two ninths!

10
00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:19.434
The denominator tells us the size of each part, so we never add denominators. Make them the same first, then add the numerators.

11
00:01:19.584 --> 00:01:29.178
Check: when you add, the answer must be bigger than each part. Two ninths is smaller than one third, so it can't be right.

12
00:01:29.328 --> 00:01:37.890
Your turn! What is two fifths plus three tenths? Pause and think.

13
00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:46.242
Two fifths is four tenths. Add three tenths and you get seven tenths. Did you get it right?

14
00:01:46.392 --> 00:01:55.218
Another one! What is seven eighths minus one quarter? Pause and think.

15
00:01:55.368 --> 00:02:04.098
One quarter is two eighths. Seven eighths minus two eighths is five eighths. Did you get it right?

16
00:02:04.248 --> 00:02:13.098
Here's another! What is three quarters plus five twelfths? Pause and think.

17
00:02:13.248 --> 00:02:23.466
Three quarters is nine twelfths. Add five twelfths to get fourteen twelfths, which is 1 and one sixth. Did you get it right?

18
00:02:23.616 --> 00:02:34.650
Last one! Someone eats half a cake, and then one sixth of it. What fraction is left? Pause and think.

19
00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:43.506
1 minus three sixths minus one sixth leaves two sixths, which is one third. Did you get it right?

20
00:02:43.656 --> 00:02:56.370
Remember: when the denominators are different, change the smaller one to match the bigger one. Then add or subtract only the numerators, simplify, and write answers greater than 1 as mixed numbers.

21
00:02:56.520 --> 00:03:02.010
You can now add and subtract fractions. Well done!

